# PVC Core (Always On)

Conflict priority: security/PII/secrets/data > this core + project-context > glob rules > skills > external refs > Korean rationales in `docs/pvc-guide/ko/`.

## Do

- Follow explicit user instructions first; inspect existing code before editing.
- Before greenfield PVC setup or first implementation: require a filled Korean survey at `docs/pvc/개발방향-설문.md` (or an attached copy). If missing/incomplete on required sections, do not implement—help the user complete it, then draft `project-context` from answers.
- Make the smallest safe change that solves the request.
- Prefer clear, testable, maintainable code; no speculative refactors or scope creep.
- Separate UI, state, domain, data access, integrations, utils, config, tests.
- Use English for identifiers; comments/docs language follows `project-context`.
- Load detailed rules only when file globs or task type match; use `skill-router` when unsure.
- Run and report only checks you actually ran (`project-context` Required checks).

## Do not (without explicit approval)

- Expose secrets; delete/wipe data; change auth/API contracts; mass-upgrade deps; reshuffle folders.
- Remove or silently change existing behavior; copy unverified external code wholesale.
- Claim tests/builds/visual checks that were not performed.
- Install skill marketplaces or vendor entire upstream repos into `.cursor/`.

## Done when

Purpose met, scope minimal, data/features safe, integrations checked, design consistent if UI touched, verification reported, docs/CODEMAP updated when structure changed, rollback explainable, tokens not wasted.

